			"id": "agent-analysis-ota-backup-restore-extension",
			"interpretation": "Single hvigor module 'entry' of the OtaBackupEx Harmony sample. Core mechanism: EntryBackupAbility extends CoreFileKit's BackupExtensionAbility with onBackup() and onRestoreEx(bundleVersion, restoreInfo); module.json5 registers it under extensionAbilities (type 'backup', srcEntry pointing at that file, metadata 'ohos.extension.backup' -> $profile:backup_config, whose JSON sets allowToBackupRestore true). onRestoreEx branches on bundleVersion.name.startsWith('0.0.0.0') for the HarmonyOS-to-NEXT migration named in comments; IsOtaScenario parses restoreInfo as a {type,detail} array, treating type=='isSameDevice' && detail=='true' as the OTA case, else clone; other versions hit an 'Other scenario' branch; returns JSON ErrorInfo with errorCode 0; unguarded JSON.parse throws on malformed restoreInfo. module.json5 also names EntryAbility mainElement, loading 'pages/Index' from main_pages.json. Maintenance: keep srcEntry/profile references, the backup_config flag, and build-profile targets ('default','ohosTest') consistent; parent OtaBackupEx/build-profile.json5 registers this module at srcPath './entry'; src/test and src/ohosTest suites are scaffolds not exercising the extension.",
